# Files every slice only appends to merge by keeping both sides (docs/testing.md § "Landing a slice").
# A union merge keeps every line both branches added.
docs/decisions.md merge=union

# Source and JSON merge through their grammar, declaration by declaration and record by record (`apq merge-file`):
# imports of both sides united, members and records both sides added kept, a layout-only difference read as none; a
# declaration both sides changed stays a conflict. `dev land` names the driver; elsewhere name it on the command line —
#   git -c merge.anyparse.driver='node bin/apq.js merge-file %O %A %B --path %P' merge <branch>
# Without the driver git falls back to its ordinary line merge.
*.hx merge=anyparse
*.json merge=anyparse
